<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boudica</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 60 or 61</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Boadicea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boudica was queen of the Iceni of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> who led a great revolt against Roman rule in 60 or 61 CE after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> seized her late husband's kingdom and mistreated her family. Her forces destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camulodunum">Camulodunum</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colchester">Colchester</a>), <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/londinium">Londinium</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verulamium">Verulamium</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-albans">St Albans</a>), killing many thousands, before the governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-suetonius-paulinus">Gaius Suetonius Paulinus</a> defeated them in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midlands">Midlands</a>. She died soon after.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boudica.jpg" alt="Boudica" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Opie · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Queen_Boudica_by_John_Opie.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
